{"id":"35","title":"At the Market","goal":"商品と数量について尋ね、価格について話し、提示された条件を受け入れるか断るかを伝えられるようになります。","language":"ja","study":[{"id":"35-study-0","title":"この章のはじめに","blocks":[{"id":"ja-35-study-0-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"まず、何の商品について聞きたいかを示します。"},{"text":"How much are the strawberries?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、いちごの値段を尋ねる質問です。その値段で買える量が分からないなら、"},{"text":"Is that per basket or per pound?","emphasis":true},{"text":" と確認します。これは、一かごあたりの値段なのか、一ポンドあたりの値段なのかを聞いています。"},{"text":"price","emphasis":true},{"text":" は代金がいくらか、"},{"text":"quantity","emphasis":true},{"text":" はどれだけの量を受け取るかです。価格だけでなく、その価格に対応する量も確認しましょう。"}],"span":[6,6],"phraseIds":["ch35-p126466145906530","ch35-p161583884324508","ch35-p2392610526555","ch35-p4441091620197"]},{"id":"ja-35-study-0-1","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"数量を表す便利なまとまりには、次のものがあります。"}],"span":[8,8],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-35-study-0-2","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"a loaf of bread","emphasis":true},{"text":"：パン一つです。ここでは、ひとかたまりのパンを数えています。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"a bunch of grapes","emphasis":true},{"text":"：ぶどう一房です。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"a jar of honey","emphasis":true},{"text":"：瓶入りのはちみつ一つです。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"a bag of apples","emphasis":true},{"text":"：りんご一袋です。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"a dozen eggs","emphasis":true},{"text":"：卵十二個です。"},{"text":"A dozen","emphasis":true},{"text":" は十二を表します。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"a pound of potatoes","emphasis":true},{"text":"：じゃがいも一ポンド分です。"}]}],"span":[10,15],"phraseIds":["ch35-p253758856275062","ch35-p38133954802087","ch35-p142991608017787","ch35-p163920673410424","ch35-p73492244729209","ch35-p135810611468"]},{"id":"ja-35-study-0-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"店頭の表示にある単位を使うか、売り手に尋ねます。重さや一袋の大きさを、自分だけで決めつけないようにしましょう。"}],"span":[17,17],"phraseIds":[]}],"line":6},{"id":"35-study-1","title":"生鮮食品を買う","blocks":[{"id":"ja-35-study-1-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"次の練習用の売り場は架空です。英語の価格設定をそのまま示します。"}],"span":[21,21],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-35-study-1-1","type":"quote","paragraphs":[[{"text":"For this fictional practice stall: strawberries cost $5 per basket; bread costs $4 per loaf; eggs cost $6 per dozen. These are scene prices, not a price guide."}]],"span":[23,23],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-35-study-1-2","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"いちごは "},{"text":"$5 per basket","emphasis":true},{"text":"（一かご5ドル）、パンは "},{"text":"$4 per loaf","emphasis":true},{"text":"（パン一つ4ドル）、卵は "},{"text":"$6 per dozen","emphasis":true},{"text":"（十二個6ドル）という設定です。この場面で計算や会話をするための価格であり、実際の相場を示すものではありません。"}],"span":[25,25],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch35-b3","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Customer","runs":[{"text":"How much are the strawberries?"}],"id":"ch35-line14","person":"Customer","en":"How much are the strawberries?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-903539973.svg"},{"speaker":"Seller","runs":[{"text":"Five dollars a basket."}],"id":"ch35-line15","person":"Seller","en":"Five dollars a basket.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-95410790.svg"},{"speaker":"Customer","runs":[{"text":"I'll take one basket and a loaf of bread, please."}],"id":"ch35-line16","person":"Customer","en":"I'll take one basket and a loaf of bread, please.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-903539973.svg"},{"speaker":"Seller","runs":[{"text":"Sure. That's nine dollars."}],"id":"ch35-line17","person":"Seller","en":"Sure. That's nine dollars.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-95410790.svg"},{"speaker":"Customer","runs":[{"text":"Can I pay by card?"}],"id":"ch35-line18","person":"Customer","en":"Can I pay by card?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-903539973.svg"},{"speaker":"Seller","runs":[{"text":"Yes, we accept cards."}],"id":"ch35-line19","person":"Seller","en":"Yes, we accept cards.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-95410790.svg"},{"speaker":"Customer","runs":[{"text":"Great. Could I have a receipt?"}],"id":"ch35-line20","person":"Customer","en":"Great. Could I have a receipt?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-903539973.svg"}],"span":[14,20],"art":"ch35-scene-0.svg","theme":"market","people":["Customer","Seller"],"caption":"生鮮食品を買う","phraseIds":["ch35-line14","ch35-line15","ch35-line16","ch35-line17","ch35-line18","ch35-line19","ch35-line20"]},{"id":"ja-35-study-1-4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"客はまずいちごの価格を聞きます。売り手は一かごの価格だと答えています。客は、いちご一かごとパン一つを選びます。合計は、上の架空の設定に基づく "},{"text":"nine dollars","emphasis":true},{"text":" です。その後、カードで支払えるかと、購入の記録をもらえるかを尋ねています。"}],"span":[35,35],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-35-study-1-5","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"I'll take it","emphasis":true},{"text":" は「それを買います」と、購入を決めたことを伝えます。"},{"text":"I'm just looking","emphasis":true},{"text":" は「今は見ているだけです」で、まだ購入を決めていないと説明します。"}],"span":[37,37],"phraseIds":["ch35-p196381242069473","ch35-p94120984187817"]},{"id":"ja-35-study-1-6","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Can I have...?","emphasis":true},{"text":"、"},{"text":"Could I have...?","emphasis":true},{"text":"、"},{"text":"I'd like...","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、いずれも欲しいものを頼むときの選択肢です。最初の形だけで、必ず丁寧、必ず失礼と決まるわけではありません。場面、声の調子、前後を含めたやり取りに合わせて使います。"}],"span":[39,39],"phraseIds":["ch35-p124432291623132","ch35-p3767619254940","ch35-p251997198343081"]}],"line":19},{"id":"35-study-2","title":"提示された価格について話す","blocks":[{"id":"ja-35-study-2-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"値段の交渉は、買い手からの価格の提案を受け付ける場面で行う会話です。どの店でもするものではありません。次の英語は架空の場面設定です。"}],"span":[43,43],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-35-study-2-1","type":"quote","paragraphs":[[{"text":"In the next fictional scene, a secondhand stall displays a sign: "},{"text":"Offers welcome","emphasis":true},{"text":". A lamp is marked $25."}]],"span":[45,45],"phraseIds":["ch35-p109079536857321"]},{"id":"ja-35-study-2-2","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"中古品売り場には、"},{"text":"Offers welcome","emphasis":true},{"text":" という表示があります。希望する価格を提案してよいという意味です。ランプには "},{"text":"$25","emphasis":true},{"text":" の値札が付いています。"}],"span":[47,47],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch35-b6","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Buyer","runs":[{"text":"Would you take twenty dollars for the lamp?"}],"id":"ch35-line28","person":"Buyer","en":"Would you take twenty dollars for the lamp?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-264961516.svg"},{"speaker":"Seller","runs":[{"text":"I could do twenty-three."}],"id":"ch35-line29","person":"Seller","en":"I could do twenty-three.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-95410790.svg"},{"speaker":"Buyer","runs":[{"text":"Twenty-three is more than I want to spend. How about twenty-one?"}],"id":"ch35-line30","person":"Buyer","en":"Twenty-three is more than I want to spend. How about twenty-one?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-264961516.svg"},{"speaker":"Seller","runs":[{"text":"Sorry, twenty-three is my lowest price."}],"id":"ch35-line31","person":"Seller","en":"Sorry, twenty-three is my lowest price.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-95410790.svg"},{"speaker":"Buyer","runs":[{"text":"Okay, I'll pass. Thanks anyway."}],"id":"ch35-line32","person":"Buyer","en":"Okay, I'll pass. Thanks anyway.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-264961516.svg"}],"span":[28,32],"art":"ch35-scene-1.svg","theme":"market","people":["Buyer","Seller"],"caption":"提示された価格について話す","phraseIds":["ch35-line28","ch35-line29","ch35-line30","ch35-line31","ch35-line32"]},{"id":"ja-35-study-2-4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"買い手は "},{"text":"twenty dollars","emphasis":true},{"text":"、つまり20ドルを提案します。売り手は "},{"text":"twenty-three","emphasis":true},{"text":"（23ドル）なら可能だと答えます。買い手は予算より高いので "},{"text":"twenty-one","emphasis":true},{"text":"（21ドル）を再提案しますが、売り手は23ドルが最も低い価格だと伝えます。最後に、買い手は購入を見送っています。"}],"span":[55,55],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-35-study-2-5","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Would you take...?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、その価格で売ることを受け入れるか尋ねます。"},{"text":"That's my lowest price","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、これ以上価格を下げないという売り手の返事です。"},{"text":"I'll pass","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、この購入を断る、見送るという意味です。"}],"span":[57,57],"phraseIds":["ch35-p226333828020869","ch35-p244676434970568","ch35-p203822655281475"]},{"id":"ja-35-study-2-6","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"断るときに、架空の理由を作る必要はありません。"},{"text":"Twenty is my limit.","emphasis":true},{"text":" なら、使える金額の上限をはっきり伝えます。受け入れるなら、"},{"text":"Okay, twenty-three works. I'll take it.","emphasis":true},{"text":" と、合意する価格と購入の意思を伝えられます。"}],"span":[59,59],"phraseIds":["ch35-p201186347655482","ch35-p195761321399668"]}],"line":41},{"id":"35-study-3","title":"買うものを確認する","blocks":[{"id":"ja-35-study-3-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"提示された価格に何が含まれるかが不明なら、"},{"text":"Does that price include both pieces?","emphasis":true},{"text":" と聞けます。これは、その価格に二つとも含まれるかという質問です。"},{"text":"Can I buy just one?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、一つだけ買えるかを尋ねます。"}],"span":[63,63],"phraseIds":["ch35-p86392317755454","ch35-p113772853428590"]},{"id":"ja-35-study-3-1","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Is this ripe?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、果物が食べ頃まで熟しているかを聞きます。"},{"text":"Could I take a closer look?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、商品を近くで見せてもらえるかを頼む言い方です。買うと決める前に、量や状態を確認できます。"}],"span":[65,65],"phraseIds":["ch35-p4947566784586","ch35-p153671901281360"]}],"line":61},{"id":"35-words","title":"言葉と表現","blocks":[{"id":"35-glossary","type":"vocabulary","phraseIds":["ch35-v0","ch35-v1","ch35-v2","ch35-v3"]}]}],"practice":[{"id":"35-practice-0","title":"自分で試す","blocks":[{"id":"ja-35-practice-0-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"一人なら、売り手の発言を読み、買い手として声に出して答えます。その後、役を逆にします。実際に買い物をする必要はありません。"}],"span":[69,69],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch35-b10","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"number":1,"runs":[{"text":"生鮮食品の売り場で、パンを二つ買います。カード払いができるか尋ねてください。計算は、上に示した架空の表示価格を使います。"}],"id":"ch35-b10-0"},{"number":2,"runs":[{"text":"Offers welcome","emphasis":true},{"text":" の売り場で、ランプに "},{"text":"$20","emphasis":true},{"text":" を提案します。売り手は "},{"text":"I can do twenty-three.","emphasis":true},{"text":" と答えます。その価格を受け入れるか、自分の上限は "},{"text":"$20","emphasis":true},{"text":" なので断るかを選んでください。"}],"id":"ch35-b10-1"},{"number":3,"runs":[{"text":"売り手が "},{"text":"They're five dollars.","emphasis":true},{"text":" と言います。一個の価格か、一かごの価格か分かりません。買うものを選ぶ前に、意味を確認してください。"}],"id":"ch35-b10-2"}],"span":[71,73],"phraseIds":[]}],"line":69,"answers":[{"id":"ja-35-practice-0-2","type":"answer","runs":[{"text":"答えの例:","emphasis":true},{"text":" “Two loaves, please.” — “That's eight dollars.” — “Can I pay by card?” / “Would you take twenty?” — “I can do twenty-three.” — “Okay, I'll take it.” または “Thanks, but twenty is my limit. I'll pass.” / “Is that five dollars each or per basket?”"}],"span":[75,75],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-35-practice-0-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"最初の例では、パンの数量を指定し、その代金を聞いてから支払い方法を確認しています。値段の交渉では、受け入れる返事と、上限を示して断る返事のどちらも使えます。最後の質問は、"},{"text":"each","emphasis":true},{"text":" が一個ずつ、"},{"text":"per basket","emphasis":true},{"text":" が一かごずつを表しています。"}],"span":[77,77],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-35-practice-0-4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"後で数量や金額の上限を変えて練習してください。買い物の終わりまでに、双方が商品、数量、合意した価格を理解できたかを確かめましょう。"}],"span":[79,79],"phraseIds":[]}]}],"phrases":[{"id":"ch35-p126466145906530","en":"How much are the strawberries?","section":"35-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch35-p126466145906530"},{"id":"ch35-p161583884324508","en":"Is that per basket or per pound?","section":"35-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch35-p161583884324508"},{"id":"ch35-p2392610526555","en":"price","section":"35-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"word","ja":"","studyId":"ch35-p2392610526555"},{"id":"ch35-p4441091620197","en":"quantity","section":"35-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"word","ja":"","studyId":"ch35-p4441091620197"},{"id":"ch35-p253758856275062","en":"a loaf of bread","section":"35-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch35-p253758856275062"},{"id":"ch35-p38133954802087","en":"a bunch of grapes","section":"35-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch35-p38133954802087"},{"id":"ch35-p142991608017787","en":"a j